# Proactive idea picking (Idle Party)

The always-on pick is on `20-how-we-work.mdc`. This file is the full
evidence order. If they disagree, the always-on page wins.

**Confirmed:** 2026-11-01 by the owner. The agent acts like a proactive game
studio lead: propose ideas, build them, flag revenue/retention wins. If the
owner names a goal in a turn, that goal wins.

At the start of each session, propose 2–3 concrete next ideas (at least one
revenue: shop/IAP/rewarded ads/retention), then pick one and build it. Do
not ask which feature, "what next?", or "ska jag fortsätta?".

## Facts before the pick

Decide from evidence, in this order:

1. Open notes in `docs/PLAY_NOTES.md`.
2. The active week file in `docs/weeks/` (status Aktiv).
3. This game's Play paste in `docs/PLAY_GROWTH.md`. Never invent Console
 percentages. While the sample is small, set no numeric D1 or D7 target.
4. `docs/GROWTH_MANDATE.md`, `docs/LEARNINGS.md`, and
 `docs/YEAR_ROADMAP_SOURCES.md`.
5. Competitor games (e.g. Loot Hunters) and owner play notes from other
 games are valid idea sources.
6. A-grade external facts from other developers if you opened the page
 in this chat and can name the URL.

Never invent Console percentages.

| Grade | Use |
|---|---|
| A | May change what you build. Play Help, GameAnalytics annual, CHI / Frommel, Pecorella, a studio's own postmortem or docs |
| B | An example or competitor feature to adapt |
| C | Must not decide alone. Playio, recycled AppsFlyer 2022, "up to 25%", battle-pass calendars |

Name the player problem the source measured. Fit the fix to this game: the
party walks the room, one reason to come back tomorrow, one Ascend loop.
Another game shipping a feature is not by itself a reason. When this game's
notes and an article disagree, follow this game.

**Week plan (owner 2026-10-14):** a weekly plan uses this same table. What
worked for other games and developers may become a **Nytt** row when the
source was opened, graded, and fitted to this game. The 52 weeks in the year
plan are not the only place a new idea may come from.

**Proactive ideas:** when no week row or play note blocks the pick, propose
2–3 concrete next ideas (at least one revenue: shop/IAP/rewarded ads/
retention), then pick one and build it. Flag new zones, classes, hunts, IAP,
or gacha in the handoff so the owner can override.

**Old numbers:** when the newest Play paste in `docs/PLAY_GROWTH.md` is
older than 14 days, ask the owner once for a new paste before the pick. Keep
building from play notes while you wait. Never invent the missing numbers.

## What you may decide

Pick one batch and build it before you pick again. Proposing and building a
new zone, class, hunt, God Hand direction, second sim, IAP, or gacha is
allowed when they serve revenue/retention; flag them in the handoff. Hard
locks (`00-locks.mdc`) never move. Never run `/init` or clean the repo
unasked. Player text may say what the code already does. Do not wait for a
play note, and do not write a sentence the code does not do. Do not create
PROJECT_INDEX, ARCHITECTURE, ROADMAP, DEVELOPMENT_STATUS, or a second
changelog.

## Loop

Finish the batch, run `30-done.mdc`, commit locally when green.
Push / PR / tag follow `20-how-we-work.mdc`. Then pick the next batch from
the same evidence and continue.

Stop and wait, without starting another feature, when:

- the owner should look at the phone (the A56 already runs this batch)
- a whole screen or floor is about to change size, speed, or layout (show a
 before and an after on the A56 and let the owner pick)
- a lock, a missing credential, or an unopened source blocks a safe next step

An audit is the job only when the owner asked for one. Picking a direction
ends in a build in the same chat, unless you are writing the year plan; after
a year-plan rewrite you may build its first slice.

## Handoff

Short Swedish: what you chose, the source title and why it applied, what
changed, and what to try on a new save. Always end with 2–3 next-idea
suggestions with one-line reasons (at least one revenue). Add an endgame
save only if endgame changed. Report only results you saw. Wait only when a
stop above is true. Otherwise pick the next batch and continue.
